==English==

===Etymology===
Since the maximum number of balls before a [[walk#baseball|walk]] is three, and the maximum number of strikes before a [[strikeout]] is two, neither number can increase without ending the at-bat.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|baseball|lang=en}} An [[at-bat]] with a count of three [[ball#baseball|balls]] and two [[strike#baseball|strikes]].
#: '' '''Full count''', two outs, bottom of the ninth, the bags are jammed, 2-2 tie...''

====Usage notes====
* occasionally used in the form ''the count is full''